  The coverage inventory records starting SHA-256 hashes. Existing evidence
  files are canonical read-only inputs; put revisions in your report
  directory. Do not edit another package's chapter, the main include file,
  shared metadata, published PDF, glossary, outline, bibliography or Lean
  source. Request a scope split for a new chapter rather than creating an
  overlapping producer.

  <section|Mathematical checks><label|mathematical-checks>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Keep full-mesh convergence separate from extraction along a
    subsequence.

    <item>Check phase disintegration, all-character versus selected
    assertions, and common field quotient/injection.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Start from existing evidence><label|start-from-existing-evidence>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|blueprint/units/YM-000026/fullmesh-correlation-cauchy-evidence.md>

